@format 1
@id media-preview.common.mpv-preview
@title mpv preview
@section Media preview
@area Common
@entry mpv-start
@summary Trace the Edit-eligible mpv path through the independent audio-only permission gate, opening/fallback, viewer-state commit, synchronous media publication, and post-publication preview/autoplay work.
@related media-preview.common.flyleaf-preview, media-preview.common.media-publication, media-preview.in-edit
@tag media
@tag preview
@tag common
@tag mpv

@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer

[mpv-start] mpv preview path <input>
~ The preview uses the selected preview engine for this path.
[Technical explanation]
= PPlayerMediaApply reached mpv only because PViewerEngineSelect previously activated mpv on a viewer whose PViewerEditEligible setting permits the configured renderer engine.
> audio-permission

[audio-permission] Independent audio-only permission <decision>
~ The program checks independent audio-only permission.
[Technical explanation]
- PViewerMpvApply checks audio-only media against the viewer's private audio-only allowance, which is configured through PViewerAudioSet; this rejection gate is separate from PViewerEditEligible @ viewer.PViewerAudioSet(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerMpvApply(...)
? "Audio-only source and audio-only not allowed" > restricted
? "Media allowed by audio-only setting" > open

[restricted] Restricted-source commit request <process>
~ The program prepares to accept a media source that has limited preview support.
[Technical explanation]
- Prepare PViewerMpvCommit with cargo that has no usable media/preview and carries the audio-only restriction @ viewer.PViewerMpvCommit(...)
> restricted-ready

[open] mpv preview opening <external>
~ The preview engine starts opening the selected media.
[Technical explanation]
- Ensure an mpv player is attached, apply volume, and open the source on a worker task @ viewer.PViewerMpvApply(...)
> open-result

[restricted-ready] Restricted mpv commit ready <junction>
> commit-join

[open-result] mpv opening result <decision>
~ The program checks whether the preview engine opened the media successfully.
[Technical explanation]
- Recheck viewer lifetime/load serial after opening and distinguish stale, failed, and ready results @ viewer.PViewerMpvApply(...)
? "Viewer request became stale" > stale
? "mpv open failed" > fallback
? "mpv preview ready" > commit-join

[commit-join] mpv commit inputs converge <junction>
> commit-state

[stale] Stale mpv result ignored <output>
~ This path ends with stale preview engine result ignored.
[Technical explanation]
= An obsolete mpv result does not replace current viewer state.

[fallback] Flyleaf fallback preparation <process>
~ This step handles preview engine fallback preparation.
[Technical explanation]
- Dispose the mpv host and build a Flyleaf host for the same source after checking current request ownership @ viewer.PViewerMpvFallback(...)
> fallback-result

[commit-state] Commit viewer identity and preview visibility <process>
~ The preview makes this media file current and updates the preview display.
[Technical explanation]
- In PViewerMpvCommit, update preview visibility, media information, PViewerSourcePath, stopped playback state, and nonpersistent crop state @ viewer.PViewerMpvCommit(...)
> publish

[fallback-result] Fallback request check <decision>
~ The program checks fallback request check.
[Technical explanation]
- Recheck load serial and viewer lifetime before retrying through Flyleaf @ viewer.PViewerMpvFallback(...)
? "Viewer request still current" > map:media-preview.common.flyleaf-preview
? "Viewer request became stale" > fallback-stale

[publish] Synchronous viewer-media publication <process>
~ The preview immediately announces that its current media changed.
[Technical explanation]
- Invoke PViewerMediaRaise before mpv preview filters, autoplay/pause, final playback-state update, or clock startup @ viewer.PViewerMediaRaise(...)
! PViewerMediaRaise returns to PViewerMpvCommit before those remaining operations continue.
> preview-check

[fallback-stale] Stale fallback ignored <output>
~ This path ends with stale fallback ignored.
[Technical explanation]
= Flyleaf fallback is not started for an obsolete viewer request.

[preview-check] Usable mpv preview present <decision>
~ The program checks usable preview engine preview present.
[Technical explanation]
- Continue according to the committed preview availability @ viewer.PViewerMpvCommit(...)
? "No usable preview" > no-preview
? "Preview ready" > apply-preview

[no-preview] Dispose unavailable player and stop <process>
~ This step handles dispose unavailable player and stop.
[Technical explanation]
- Dispose the player and publish stopped-at-zero playback state after media publication @ viewer.PViewerMpvCommit(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerPlaybackUpdate(...)
> no-preview-wait-one

[apply-preview] Apply mpv preview filters <process>
~ This step handles apply preview engine preview filters.
[Technical explanation]
- Apply current preview filter state after media publication @ viewer.PViewerMpvPreviewApply(...)
> autoplay-check

[no-preview-wait-one] No-preview alignment one <junction>
> no-preview-wait-two

[autoplay-check] Autoplay preference <decision>
~ The program checks autoplay preference.
[Technical explanation]
- Branch on the autoplay preference only after mpv preview filters are applied @ viewer.PViewerMpvCommit(...)
? "Autoplay enabled" > autoplay
? "Autoplay disabled" > paused

[no-preview-wait-two] No-preview alignment two <junction>
> complete-join

[autoplay] Start mpv playback <process>
~ This step handles start preview engine playback.
[Technical explanation]
- Play, publish current playing/time state, and start the viewer clock @ viewer.PViewerMpvCommit(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerPlaybackUpdate(...)
> complete-join

[paused] Keep mpv paused <process>
~ This step handles keep preview engine paused.
[Technical explanation]
- Pause and publish stopped-at-zero playback state @ viewer.PViewerMpvCommit(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerPlaybackUpdate(...)
> complete-join

[complete-join] mpv completion convergence <junction>
> mpv-complete

[mpv-complete] mpv commit finished <output>
~ The preview has finished switching to the new media.
[Technical explanation]
= Viewer-media subscribers ran before final mpv preview/playback state was applied.
